<title>FINLAND: FINNISH APR TIMBER CUTTINGS UP 37 PCT YR/YR - METLA.</title>
<headline>FINNISH APR TIMBER CUTTINGS UP 37 PCT YR/YR - METLA.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of raw timber cuttings increased 37 percent year-on-year in April to 4.7 million cubic metres, the Finnish Forest Research Institute (METLA) said in a review on Friday.</p>
<p>Logwood timber cuttings increased 38 percent to 2.1 million cubic metres -- 10 percent above average -- and pulpwood timber cuttings rose 37 percent to 2.6 million cubic metres -- 11 percent above average, Metla said.</p>
<p>Of total April timber cuttings, 87 percent or 4.1 million cubic metres, took place in privately-owned forests, it said.</p>
<p>The volume of raw timber cuttings in January-April rose 14 percent year-on-year to 20.1 cubic metres, METLA said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 240, news@reuter.fi</p>
